  "step_2": "The verbal report states: 'B, sicherer relativ hoher Gewinn', which translates to 'B, safer relatively high win'. The individual emphasizes safety (certainty) and describes the outcome of B as a 'relatively high win'. This suggests that the person considered the outcomes of the lotteries and judged the outcome of B to be sufficiently good (high enough) and preferred it due to its certainty. The individual appears to focus on the guaranteed nature of the outcome in B and views it as a favorable result. There is no mention of detailed calculations or outcome comparisons beyond characterizing B’s outcome as a 'relatively high win' and emphasizing its safety.",
